        /// <remarks>
        /// Adds finished trials to a run opened with `finalize: false`, so a job started from MKA1 can be watched while it runs instead of appearing complete out of nowhere at the end. Each trial pins its own `sample_index` and upserts on (task, model, sample_index): a harness cannot tell a timeout from a lost response, so re-sending a batch is safe and replaces rather than duplicates. The whole batch and its aggregate recompute land in one transaction, serialized per run. Counts, metrics and cost are recomputed from the stored rows on every call, never accumulated from the request, so a replayed batch cannot double them. Send `finalize: true` (usually with an empty `trials`) to close the run — until then it stays `in_progress` and off the leaderboards, which only count completed runs. Appending to an already-completed or cancelled run is rejected: that record is finished, and rewriting it would silently move a number someone may have already read.<br/>
